{"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"ISSUE_TEXT_PRIVACY","classStatement":"The filing criterion omits a required protection for client names.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"Design line 134 prohibits client names in filed issue text. AC5 (lines 111–123) requires path redaction and excludes other configured repository names, but does not prohibit client names; R5 (line 172) likewise has no client-name check.","failureScenario":"A finding’s class or failure scenario contains a client name -> a new-work decision copies that free text into a GitHub issue, disclosing the name despite the approved design constraint.","id":"F1","severity":"high"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"AMBIGUOUS_REPOSITORY_ROUTING","classStatement":"Review follow-ups lack a testable rule for selecting the issue repository.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC1 (lines 58–61) defines no repository field for a review follow-up, while AC5 (lines 111–121) requires filing in the follow-up’s repository without defining how that repository is selected. R5 (line 172) tests filing but not repository routing.","failureScenario":"A run has two configured repositories and a review follow-up needs new work -> implementations can choose different repositories, and an issue may be filed in the wrong one.","id":"F2","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"ORIGIN_SHAPE_MISMATCH","classStatement":"The non-review input and recorded origin are inconsistent or insufficiently specified against the design.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"Design lines 51–57 place repository, manifest, vulnerability, package, version, severity, title and preExisting in the dependency-scan origin. AC2 (lines 73–84) instead requires those fields on each finding and only says the record has the AC1 fields 'where they apply'; R2 (line 169) does not verify the recorded origin shape.","failureScenario":"The dependency-scan gate supplies the origin shape described by the approved design -> the API may reject it for missing per-finding fields, or record a follow-up whose origin lacks the required provenance.","id":"F3","severity":"medium"},{"blocking":true,"classId":"REOPENED_METRICS_STALE","classStatement":"Metrics criteria do not account for decisions invalidated by reopening.","document":"requirements/spec.md","evidence":"AC1 (lines 67–69) says reopening makes a follow-up undecided and earlier decisions no longer count. AC9 (lines 145–153) says the metrics row takes the latest decided status, without a reopening reset; R9 (line 176) does not test reopening.","failureScenario":"A decided finding is fixed and later re-reported before a new decision -> status shows undecided while the metrics projection can retain the old decision and report it as decided.","id":"F4","severity":"medium"}],"mandateAssessment":null,"outcome":"FAIL","summary":"The spec is not ready to authorize implementation. Issue filing lacks a defined repository selection rule and omits the design’s client-name protection; the non-review record shape and reopened-finding metrics also need clarification and rubric coverage."}